        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಹೊಡೆದಾಟ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೊಡೆದಾಟ — hoḍedāṭa — \"a fistfight; a brawl\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪಂದ್ಯದ ನಂತರ ಎರಡು ಗುಂಪುಗಳ ನಡುವೆ ಹೊಡೆದಾಟ ಆಯಿತು. pandyada nantara eraḍu gumpugaḷa naḍuve hoḍedāṭa āyitu. After the match there was a fight between two groups."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೊಡೆದು, having hit, and ಆಟ, play: hitting back and forth. The verb is ಹೊಡೆದಾಡು, to come to blows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೊಡೆದಾಟ (hoḍedāṭa) is a native Dravidian compound: ಹೊಡೆದು, \"having struck\", from hoḍe, \"to strike, to beat\" (DEDR 4252), and ಆಟ, \"play\", from āḍu (DEDR 347)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
