          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೈದಿ — kaidi — \"a prisoner\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ರಾತ್ರಿ ಒಬ್ಬ ಕೈದಿ ಸೆರೆಮನೆಯಿಂದ ತಪ್ಪಿಸಿಕೊಂಡನು. rātri obba kaidi seremaneyinda tappisikoṇḍanu. At night a prisoner escaped from the prison."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ಕೈದಿಗಳು, kaidigaḷu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A prisoner is held in a ಸೆರೆಮನೆ, a prison; ಕೈದಿ (kaidi) ಸಂಖ್ಯೆ is his number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೈದಿ (kaidi) is a loan from Arabic qaidī, \"a captive, a prisoner\", which came through Persian and Hindustani."
            }
          ]
        },
